The Honourable Duty of         NannyMUD Times                         Page 8
the Deputy by Hisashi

Basalt Keep attacks. A knight's view.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Greetings.
  
  I admit not being around when the first Basalt Keep attacks
  appeared.
  
  I am a new member of the defenders of Basalt Keep, the Deputies.
  As a Deputy it is my duty to serve and protect,
  to defend the innocents of the proud outpost on Antharis.
  
  Many are our foes, strong are the invaders.
  The evil servants of Molt are not only cunning,
  but often much more difficult to fight and defeat
  than what I am used to in the defense of Camelot.
  Defending the Keep requires skill, strategy, great courage and speed.
  It is not an easy life, and it would be much easier to just
  abandon the Keep to it's fate, to train skills, gain money and experience
  on my own, without the need to go and protect not very
  defensible jungle outpost invaded by monstrous beings from time to time.
  
  Why then do we Deputies risk life and limb for these people?
  We do it out of honour, a strong sense of duty and
  the desire to protect the innocent, even though it is inconvenient.
  
  Our foes are strong, hellfire, balrogs and evil wizards
  seek to destroy and burn down the temple of Lars.
  
  It is the duty of all good men and women with courage and honour
  to join us in the defense of Basalt Keep.
  To brave the fires, to walk into the burning inferno and to
  fight together against the servants of evil itself.
  That is our goal, that is our duty.
  Honour and glory, strength within and without.

  Hisashi.
